   {'title':'Copilot code review effort levels are generally available','url':'https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-07-copilot-code-review-effort-levels-are-generally-available/','source_type':'release','published_or_updated':'2026-08-07','why_selected':'GA effort levels make review depth a deliberate policy choice rather than an invisible model setting.','usefulness':'Map Lite and Balanced review to change risk in a client or Buildn repository.','what':'GitHub Copilot code review now offers GA Lite and Balanced effort levels, configurable per review or as organization defaults.','matters':'Routine documentation edits and cross-service or security-sensitive changes should not consume the same review budget.','use':'Set a default for routine changes; require Balanced on sensitive paths, migrations, and externally exposed code.','caveat':'Review effort is not an acceptance test. Preserve CI, human ownership, and security review for high-consequence changes.','action':'Write a one-page PR risk rubric that assigns Lite, Balanced, or human-only review.'},
